  "full_text": "started in drywall. So like Danny went into drywall, taping, taping drywall. They had a company in Kennewick, a drywall company. Teresa ran the company and Mike did stuff. I think they went bankrupt. Everything crashed, you know. And there's Danny. Let's see. So like, that's our house right there. We started in a prefab house. The city was made in a hurry, like military. Like they used prefabricated houses that floated down the river. So there's all these, it was a duplex. And we had the, it was, I don't know, 2201 Van Giesen or something. And so we started out in kind of a crappy house and then moved into the six bedroom. And where is it? Yeah, dad had a couple of relatives, got inherited oil money and stuff. And he had a, dad's an only child, so he had an inheritance there. and he had an uncle who didn't have any kids so uncle hugh or something like that they came from texas and they had oil money a little bit one of my my godfather uncle uh chick uh mo what's his name mo turner was uh he was he was the he he worked for texico and he uh aunt margaret married a protestant it's kind of kind of a uh that's my so my my my mom came from a family of six they they had and his My grandpa Collins owned a bunch of laundromats in Houston in, I don't know, six or something. And so like Aunt Margaret, my mom graduated valedictorian from a Catholic high school or something. And she went on a girls' state. And anyway, she taught accounting. like where her students were about the same age and they used to flirt or something.",
